WasmFS: pipes report S_IFREG instead of S_IFIFO

fstat() on either end of a pipe() said regular file, so code that tells
pipes apart by S_ISFIFO() took them for files.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-pipe-fifo-mode.md

diff --git a/system/lib/wasmfs/pipe_backend.h b/system/lib/wasmfs/pipe_backend.h
index 3336f28..1d28248 100644
--- a/system/lib/wasmfs/pipe_backend.h
+++ b/system/lib/wasmfs/pipe_backend.h
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ public:
   // PipeFiles do not have or need a backend. Pass NullBackend to the parent for
   // that.
   PipeFile(mode_t mode, std::shared_ptr<PipeData> data)
-    : DataFile(mode, NullBackend), data(data) {
+    : DataFile(mode, NullBackend, S_IFIFO), data(data) {
     // Reads are always from the front; writes always to the end.
     seekable = false;
   }
